  "title": "Account details are easier to find",
  "summary": "Account menus got more useful, model health found its own endpoint, and the community filled the app catalog with developer tools.\n\nEnter and the app user menu gained shared account identity and Pollen displays. App users can see a key’s remaining budget or limit status, open Permissions, buy Pollen, and disconnect. The Usage and Earnings cards also have steadier empty states when a selected period has no data.\n\nCommunity additions include DCORE, a Discord–Telegram image bot, and five Build apps for generating regexes, converting code, writing SQL, drafting unit tests, and sketching API endpoints. Pollen Craft also joined the README showcase.\n\nCheckout now requests optional 3D Secure authentication for first purchases and packs under $10, without requiring cards to support it. Scheduled fraud scans remain read-only, with actions left to manual review.",
